                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "102459146",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198000900149",
                            "num_reviews": 188,
                            "playtime_forever": 289,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 289,
                            "last_played": 1636414195
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It's an odd game.  It takes a long time to actually start getting tricky, and at all times it kind of feels like it's dragging out the game's length with how slowly new mechanics are introduced and combined.  The character controls really awkwardly, especially on the sloped surfaces, and the isometric view, while nice to look most of the time, very often makes it WAY harder to actually solve the puzzles because there's rarely an easily-visible reference grid for heights and you can't spin the camera around to different angles to check heights or distances.  The story is also hit or miss as it has no real dialogue, so you have to really just intuit what's going on based on context you pick up.\n\nHowever, the presentation is generally pretty great, and the puzzles are fun thinkers particularly once you get to the trickier ones (and if you get stuck there's a hint system though it's sometimes less than helpful).  None of the other issues (apart from the movement and isometric view) really get in the way if you really get into the groove.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1636415380,
